  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\nA brisk westerly flow aloft continues to reside over the CWA this\nmorning. This has resulted in a few strong wind gusts over the\nnorthern Rockies and in the Cut Bank area. The strong winds should\ndiminish later this morning, but it will remain windy over much of\nNorth Central MT until this evening. Temperatures will be mild\ntoday, but expect cooler air to move into the CWA tonight as\ncooler air slowly moves southward into the CWA from Canada. \n\nSome light precip is possible tonight into Wednesday along the\ndivide, but any precipitation east of the divide should be light.\n\nOverall both the GFS/EC seem to be in better agreement through the\nforecast period. Thus after a few cooler days mid week, another\nwarming trend is expected to start again by the weekend. Any\nprecipitation over the next several days will be light, with most\nareas staying dry.\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\nDense fog around West Yellowstone this morning should begin to\nthin out between 8 and 9 AM.\n\nWind gusts this morning of 65 to 75 mph have been reported around\nEast Glacier Park and Browning, with gusts near 60 mph by Cut\nBank. Thus the high wind warning will continue for these areas,\nwith windy conditions still likely this afternoon.  \n\nBecause of lower humidity this afternoon over the eastern portions\nof the CWA, elevated fire weather conditions are possible during\nthe afternoon hours today. Brusda",
